{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.Grind.vcgen\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgen</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`vcgen` step for `sym => …` blocks. No `with` clause: compose with subsequent grind\nsteps using `<;>` instead.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.Grind.vcgen","kind":"def","line":94,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.Grind.vcgen","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L94-L102"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgen\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgen</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`vcgen` will break down a Hoare triple proof goal like `⦃P⦄ prog ⦃Q⦄` into verification conditions,\nprovided that all functions used in `prog` have specifications registered with `@[spec]`.\n\n`vcgen` is experimental and subject to change. `set_option experimental.vcgen true` acknowledges\nits experimental status and silences the warning that each call reports.\n\n### Program types\n\n`vcgen` works on any program type `Prog` that carries a `Std.WP.WP` interpretation. A monad\nis one such program type. An inductive type of commands is another, once its weakest precondition is\ndefined in terms of an operational semantics.\n\n### Verification conditions and specifications\n\nA verification condition is an entailment `pre ⊑ post` in the assertion lattice of the goal. The\noriginal program `prog` no longer occurs in it. The assertion lattice is any `CompleteLattice`, and\nthe entailment is its order, so a verification condition is an ordinary Lean goal that `grind` can\nattack.\n\nA `@[spec]` theorem declares a specification in one of two forms. A Hoare triple\n`foo_spec : ⦃P⦄ foo a b c ⦃Q⦄` states it directly. An equation `baz_eq : baz a b c = ...` states it\nby rewriting.\n\n### Features\n\nWhen used like `vcgen [foo_spec, bar_def, baz_eq]`, `vcgen` will additionally\n\n* add a Hoare triple specification `foo_spec : ⦃P⦄ foo ... ⦃Q⦄` to the `spec` set for a function\n  `foo` occurring in `prog`,\n* unfold a definition `def bar_def ... := ...` in `prog`,\n* rewrite with an equational specification `baz_eq : baz ... = ...` in `prog`.\n\n### Config options\n\nSee `Lean.Elab.Tactic.Do.VCGen.Config` for the options. Of particular note are `stepLimit = some 42`,\nwhich is useful for bisecting bugs and tracing execution, and `errorOnMissingSpec := false`, which\nleaves a goal whose head has no matching spec as a verification condition for you to discharge.\n\n### Extended syntax\n\nOften, `vcgen` will be used like this:\n```\nvcgen [...] invariants\n· I1\n· I2\nwith try finish\n```\nThe `with` clause takes one step of `grind` mode, such as `finish`. That step shares the E-graph that\n`vcgen` builds, so it sees the hypotheses of every verification condition. A sequence of steps needs\nexplicit grouping, as in `with (s₁; s₂)`.\n\nInvariants also take a labelled form, which is useful for naming inaccessibles:\n```\nvcgen [...] invariants\n| inv1 _ acc _ => I1 acc\n| _ => I2\n```\n\n`vcgen` has two further clauses.\n\n```\nvcgen until f a _ c\n```\nstops VC generation at the first program that matches the pattern, and leaves that program in the\ngoal. Holes are written `_`, as in `conv in`.\n\n```\nvcgen frames\n| f a _ c => F\n```\nsupplies a frame for a call. Take `mkFreshNat : StateM (Nat × Nat) Nat`, which returns `s.1` and\nincrements it. Its specification mentions `s.1` alone:\n```\n@[spec] theorem mkFreshNat_spec :\n    ⦃fun s => ⌜s.1 = n⌝⦄ mkFreshNat ⦃fun r s => ⌜r = n ∧ s.1 = n + 1⌝⦄\n```\nA caller that knows `s.2 = 7` loses that fact at the call, because the postcondition says nothing\nabout `s.2`. Writing\n```\nvcgen frames\n| mkFreshNat => fun s => ⌜s.2 = 7⌝\n```\ncarries `s.2 = 7` past the call, and `vcgen` proves that `mkFreshNat` preserves it. The named binders\nare in scope in the frame, bound to the matched arguments.\n\n### Invariant suggestions\n\n`vcgen [...] invariants?` warns that invariant suggestions are not available in `vcgen` and that\nthe keyword is slated for removal. Alternatives after `invariants?` elaborate like `invariants`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgen","kind":"def","line":83,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgen","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L83-L90"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeTactic\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgenDischargeTactic</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeTactic","kind":"def","line":81,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeTactic","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L81-L81"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeGrind\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgenDischargeGrind</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeGrind","kind":"def","line":80,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischargeGrind","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L80-L80"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischarge.quot\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgenDischarge</span>.<span class=\"name\">quot</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischarge.quot","kind":"def","line":73,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.vcgenDischarge.quot","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L73-L79"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Category.vcgenDischarge\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Category</span>.<span class=\"name\">vcgenDischarge</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Notation.html#Lean.Parser.Category\">Category</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The discharging step in `vcgen … with`. It is a single `grind`-mode tactic (e.g. `finish`,\n`intro`) so it can share `vcgen`'s internalised E-graph. The `tactic` alternative is a\nlower-priority catch-all so that a non-`grind` step (e.g. `with grind`, `with simp`) still parses\nand the elaborator can report a helpful error instead of a raw `expected grind` parser error.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Category.vcgenDischarge","kind":"def","line":73,"name":"Lean.Parser.Category.vcgenDischarge","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L73-L79"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.frameAlt\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">frameAlt</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"A single `frames` alternative `| f a _ c => frame`: a program pattern (a head identifier applied to\nbinder or `_` arguments, matched like the `until` pattern) and the frame assertion to apply when the\nspec for that program is used during VC generation. The named binders (e.g. `a`, `c`) are in scope\nin `frame`, bound to the matched arguments.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.frameAlt","kind":"def","line":62,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.frameAlt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L62-L68"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantAlts\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">invariantAlts</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"After `mvcgen [...]`, there can be an optional `invariants` followed by either\n* a bulleted list of invariants `· term; · term`.\n* a labelled list of invariants `| inv1 => term; inv2 a b c => term`, which is useful for naming\n  inaccessibles.\nThe tracing variant ` invariants? ` will suggest a skeleton for missing invariants; see the\ndocstring for `mvcgen`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantAlts","kind":"def","line":52,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantAlts","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L52-L60"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantsKW\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">invariantsKW</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Either the contextual keyword ` invariants ` or its tracing form ` invariants? ` which suggests\nskeletons for missing invariants as a hint.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantsKW","kind":"def","line":46,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantsKW","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L46-L50"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantCaseAlt\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">invariantCaseAlt</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"An invariant alternative of the form `| inv<n> a b c => term`, one per invariant goal.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantCaseAlt","kind":"def","line":41,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantCaseAlt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L41-L44"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantDotAlt\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">invariantDotAlt</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"An invariant alternative of the form `· term`, one per invariant goal.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantDotAlt","kind":"def","line":36,"name":"Lean.Parser.Tactic.invariantDotAlt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L36-L39"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Attr.spec\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">Attr</span>.<span class=\"name\">spec</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Marks a specification for the `vcgen` tactic.\n\n* On a theorem `foo_spec : ⦃P⦄ foo a b c ⦃Q⦄`, `vcgen` uses `foo_spec` for calls to `foo`.\n* On a definition `foo` or an equation that `@[simp]` accepts, `vcgen` rewrites calls with its\n  equations.","docLink":"./Std/WP/Tactic.html#Lean.Parser.Attr.spec","kind":"def","line":23,"name":"Lean.Parser.Attr.spec","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/Tactic.lean#L23-L30"}}],"imports":["Init.Grind.Interactive","Init.NotationExtra"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.WP.Tactic"}